{
  "id": "ss.relic.camo",
  "name": "Dead leaf",
  "description": "A dead leaf with two legs folded under it, painted for the near half and drawn as nothing but a contour for the far one — the silhouette continues, the leaf does not. The ability is not being found, and this is the hard-edged way to say it: an object that is definitely there and then definitely is not, rather than one faded evenly along its length, which at this size is just a faint object. Three earlier passes did fade it and each came out as mud on a dark plate. The rib is the darkest mark on the leaf rather than the brightest, which is what it was in the first pass, where it read as a needle driven through the middle.",
